{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788267940,"nonce":"RNzb+nveuuyaQTqi7UF4bP3X940=","title":"Session 13 live-bench finding (bench `20260901T121508`), verified against the decompiled 1.6 source. Deterministic, so it lands at the mod rung per DESIGN's 2026-09-01 ruling. Remedy decided by Evan, 2026-09-01: **`buildable:true` is OPT-IN**; the god-hand default stays.","message":"**PlaceWorkers run on the blueprint path only.** `RimWorld/GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt` ends with a loop over `entDef.PlaceWorkers[l].AllowsPlacing(...)` and returns the first refusal. `Verse/GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt` — the gate `DevVerbs.SpawnThing` uses for `mode:\"direct\"` + `ThingCategory.Building` — runs, in order: `ThingDef.CanSpawnAt` (virtual, `return true`), per-cell `InBounds`, `Walkable` and the `SpawningWipes` scan (both keyed on the CENTRE cell, a quirk `WhyNoSpawn` already documents), `edificeGrid` only when `canWipeEdifices` is false, `CanBuildOnTerrain`, `InteractionCellStandable`, `NotBlockingAnyInteractionCells`. **No PlaceWorker anywhere.** CONFIRMED.\n\nOne correction to the finding as stated: `CanSpawnAt` DOES check the new thing's own interaction cell (`InteractionCellStandable`) — that is why the granite refused at all. What it skips is the PlaceWorker half: `PlaceWorker_PreventInteractionSpotOverlap` (two benches sharing a chair-spot), and every other rule in the `PlaceWorker_*` family — `NotUnderRoof` (solar, wind), `Cooler`/`Vent` (must sit in a wall), `OnSteamGeyser`, `NeverAdjacentTrap`, `NeverAdjacentSameDef`, `MustBeIndoors`, `FuelingPort`, `WindTurbine`, `Conduit`, `MultiCellDoor` and the rest. It also skips what `CanPlaceBlueprintAt` checks before the PlaceWorkers: fog (`CannotPlaceInUndiscovered`), `InNoBuildEdgeArea`, `IdenticalThingExists`, the `MonumentMarker` rule, and `SpaceAlreadyOccupied` — because it wipes instead.\n\n**Dev staging vanishes what a player must deconstruct.** The mod passes `canWipeEdifices: true`, so a wall or rock in the footprint passes the gate, then `GenSpawn.Spawn(..., WipeMode.VanishOrMoveAside)` runs `CheckMoveItemsAside` (items relocated `Near`) and `WipeExistingThings`, which calls `item2.Destroy(DestroyMode.Vanish)` on everything `SpawningWipes` names — rock walls, player walls, other buildings. No refund, no deconstruct job, no journal line naming what was erased. On the bench, had the interaction cell been clear, the `HiTechResearchBench` spawn at `[125,128]` would have erased the granite at `[124,128]` silently (the footprint of a 5x2 about that centre spans x 123..127; `accs13-009-findrect` puts granite at 124,128).\n\n**Every dev-staged building is therefore an untested claim about what 3.3 could produce**, and the three other staging routes are worse:\n- `dev:starter-kit` → `DevVerbs.SpawnThing` (same path, and it passes no `mode`, so a building goes through `ThingPlaceMode.Near`, which is where M1's `placed:0` research bench came from — `RUNS/m1-20260831/summary.md`).\n- `world-fixture` `bench` step → `WorldFixtureVerbs.FindClearRect` (edifice/standable/zone/`Heavy`, footprint only) then `GenSpawn.Spawn(..., WipeMode.Vanish)` with **no gate at all**.\n- `JournalVerbs.SpawnPlayerBuilding` → `GenSpawn.Spawn(..., WipeMode.Vanish)`, no gate.\n\nThe other half of \"could a colonist ever build it\" is the widget gate — research, tech level, difficulty, `PlaceWorker.IsBuildDesignatorVisible` — which lives in `Designator_Build.Visible`, not in either validator. `1adc737` #3/#4 already own that finding (through `WorldSafe.Finished`, never `IsResearchFinished`); this issue reuses it.\n\n\n**1. `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}`** (buildings; `bad-args` on anything else). Runs the shared site routine from `\u003cF1 issue\u003e` — `GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt(def, pos, rot, map, godMode:false, stuffDef:stuff)` plus the `Designator_Build.Visible` clauses — BEFORE spawning. A refusal is `failed[]` in today's shape with the game's sentence as `reason` and the refusing cell as `blocker` (`\u003cF3 issue\u003e`), journaled like any other refusal. On acceptance it spawns with `VanishOrMoveAside`: after a passed blueprint check the only occupants left are the ones `CanPlaceBlueprintOver` allows (haulable items, plants, replaceable blueprints), and moving/vanishing those IS what construction would have done. The result carries `buildable:true` and a `gate` block naming which validator passed, so a fixture can prove its own provenance. Needs a `rot` argument — there is none today (`thing.Rotation` is whatever `MakeThing` left). Default unchanged: `buildable:false` keeps the god-hand, but the result gains `wiped[]` — every thing `WipeExistingThings` destroyed, in `Blockers.Describe` shape — so erasing a wall is never silent even when it is intended. Also: `canWipeEdifices:true` stays on the god-hand path only; buildable mode does not pass it.\n\n**2. `site-audit {rect?|around?, faction?}`** — a READ. For every `Building` of the player faction in the rect (default: the whole map), re-run the same routine with `thingToIgnore: the building itself` and list the ones it would refuse: `{id, def, at, rot, reason, tier}`. This is how a staged template — by any of the four routes above, or by `place-layout --mode instant` — proves it is a state 3.3's blueprint mode could have produced. The read is a heuristic and must say so in its result: a real game can legitimately reach states the validator would now refuse (a roof built over a solar panel later, an item hauled onto an interaction spot), so a hit means \"check this\", not \"this is fake\". Fog is exempt when the caller says so (`fog_exempt` in the result, the same flag `dev:*` already publishes).\n\n**3. The other routes adopt the gate**: `world-fixture` `bench` and `JournalVerbs.SpawnPlayerBuilding` route through the same helper with `buildable:true` semantics (they exist to build player-realistic fixtures; a refusal there is a fixture bug worth seeing). `dev:starter-kit` passes `mode:\"direct\"` for buildings (fixing the M1 `placed:0` shape in passing) and forwards `buildable` from its own args.\n\n\n- `dev:spawn-thing {def:\"SolarGenerator\", buildable:true}` under a roof is REFUSED with the game's `PlaceWorker_NotUnderRoof` sentence; the same call without `buildable` places it and reports `wiped:[]`. Same pair for a second research bench whose interaction cell coincides with an existing one: refused with `InteractionSpotOverlaps` vs placed.\n- `dev:spawn-thing {def:\"Wall\", buildable:false}` onto a rock wall: placed, and `wiped[0]` names the rock with `removal:\"mine\"`. With `buildable:true`: refused, `SpaceAlreadyOccupied`, blocker the rock.\n- `buildable:true` on an unresearched def (e.g. `HiTechResearchBench` on a fresh quicktest map) is refused naming the research gate, through `WorldSafe.Finished`, and the refusal is distinguishable from a placement refusal by field, not by parsing the sentence.\n- `site-audit` over a base staged god-hand with the two bad placements above lists exactly those two, each with the reason `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}` gave; after restaging them with `buildable:true` the audit over the same rect is empty. Run it once over the M1 save (`RUNS/m1-20260831/saves`) and record what it finds as evidence, not as a check.\n- The existing suites' spawn steps (3.4, 3.5, 3.6, 4087644, s13) run unchanged — the default did not move — and the closing comment lists every `GenSpawn`/`GenPlace` call site in the mod with its gate after this change, the audit `acee526` asks for extended to wipe mode.\n- `rot` is honoured: a `(5,2)` def spawned `rot:\"East\"` reads back a 2x5 occupied rect.\n- Zero red errors.\n\n`1adc737` (3.3 instant mode IS this verb with `buildable:true`; its \"instant ≡ built-blueprint\" bullet becomes provable via `site-audit`), `acee526` (same file, same call-site audit; slide and wipe are the two ways placement lies), `\u003cF1 issue\u003e` (shared routine), `\u003cF3 issue\u003e` (blocker cell). Evidence: journal `20260901T121508.ndjson` seq 38, `results/accs13-026-devspawnthing.json`, `accs13-009-findrect.json`.","files":null}]}